---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Executive AI Program — Nairon"
  description="A hands-on AI training program for founders, operators, and executives at property management businesses. Leave with a clear AI roadmap and the judgment to execute it."
  eyebrow="AI Training"
  heading="Executive AI Program"
  intro="For leaders who need to set AI strategy and see it through &mdash; not just hear about it. A working program that turns AI from a talking point into a plan your business can run.">
  <div class="page-body">
    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">Founders, operators, and executives at property management businesses who own the outcome, not just the org chart.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-3">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Founders</div>
          <h3>Own the strategy</h3>
          <p>You decide where the business places its bets. You want to understand where AI actually creates value before you commit budget and headcount to it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Operators</div>
          <h3>Run the work</h3>
          <p>You know where time and margin leak out of daily operations &mdash; permits, dispatch, quoting, follow-ups. You want to know which of those AI can take on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Executives</div>
          <h3>Set the direction</h3>
          <p>You are accountable for results across the company. You need a clear-eyed view of what AI can and cannot do, so you can lead the change instead of reacting to it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">What it covers</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">Four areas, worked through against your own operation &mdash; not slides about someone else's.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Leverage</div>
          <h3>Where AI creates real leverage in your operation</h3>
          <p>We map your workflows and find where AI removes real work &mdash; the repetitive, high-volume tasks inside your CRM, scheduling, and inbox. You leave knowing where the value is, not where the hype is.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Prioritization</div>
          <h3>How to evaluate and prioritize opportunities</h3>
          <p>Not every task is worth automating. You learn a simple way to score opportunities by impact, effort, and risk, so you spend on the work that pays back first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Operating model</div>
          <h3>Building an AI operating model</h3>
          <p>AI that does operational work needs scoped access, clear ownership, and audit. We cover how AI employees fit alongside your team, what stays human, and how you keep control.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Change</div>
          <h3>Leading the change with your team</h3>
          <p>Adoption fails on people, not technology. You leave with a plan for how to introduce AI to your team, set expectations, and bring your operators along instead of around them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Format</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">Hands-on working sessions, grounded in your actual business.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Working, not lecturing</div>
          <h3>Built around your operation</h3>
          <p>We work through your real workflows, your real tools, and your real bottlenecks. Every exercise produces something you can use, not a generic case study.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">For decision-makers</div>
          <h3>Kept at the leadership level</h3>
          <p>The program is built for the people who set direction and hold the budget. It stays focused on decisions and strategy, not tooling for its own sake.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:20px;">Scope, scheduling, and depth are set with you before we start, based on your business and who needs to be in the room. Talk to us and we will shape the program around your operation.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Outcomes</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">You leave with a plan and the judgment to run it.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">A clear roadmap</div>
          <h3>An AI roadmap for your business</h3>
          <p>A prioritized, written view of where AI goes to work in your operation first, what it touches, and what to expect &mdash; something you can act on and share with your team.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">The judgment to execute</div>
          <h3>The judgment to see it through</h3>
          <p>You leave able to tell a real opportunity from a distraction, ask the right questions of any vendor, and lead the rollout instead of outsourcing the thinking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Start with an audit</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">The best way to see where the program would take your business is to look at your operation with us.</p>
      <a href="/#book" style="align-items:center; background-color:#0f6bd4; border-radius:40px; color:#fff; display:inline-flex; font-family:'Geist',system-ui,sans-serif; font-size:15px; font-weight:500; gap:8px; margin-top:8px; padding:13px 24px; text-decoration:none;">Book an AI audit <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
